   "i": 24525,
   "title": "Cohort Builder webhooks timing out and not firing",
   "description": "We are seeing critical issues with the Cohort Builder in our production EU-Central environment. Specifically, webhooks are not firing at all, and when we try to trigger them manually, we hit timeouts immediately. This is impacting about 1677 users who rely on these updates for their workflows. Please investigate why the Cohort Builder is failing to dispatch events properly."
  },
  {
   "i": 24526,
   "title": "High latency and DB timeout in Payment Gateway v2 (Staging)",
   "description": "We are experiencing significantly high latency in the Payment Gateway v2 staging environment in the ME region. API responses are taking much longer than usual, and we are consistently hitting database query timeouts when processing transactions. This is affecting one specific test account but is blocking our QA team from proceeding with integration tests. The latency spikes seem to occur during peak load simulation."
  },
  {
   "i": 24527,
   "title": "Permission Engine audit logs missing due to improper access review",
   "description": "There is a moderate impact issue in the production Permission Engine within the EU-Central region. We are observing elevated privileges for certain user roles, and the audit logs are missing entries that should document these changes. We think it's definitely because of an improper access review process on our end that wasn't synced correctly, leading to these discrepancies. Please fix the logging gaps and privilege escalations."
  },
  {
   "i": 24528,
   "title": "Overcharging customers via Payment Gateway v2",
   "description": "We have a high-impact issue in the production Payment Gateway v2 (ME region) where customers are being overcharged. The charges appear on the final invoice, but we are unsure if the gateway itself is calculating the wrong amount or if the usage metrics being sent for billing are inflated. This affects approximately 646 users and is causing significant support volume. We need to know if the error is in the payment processing logic or the data feeding into it."
  },
  {
   "i": 24529,
   "title": "Subscription renewal failure and incorrect proration in Staging",
   "description": "In our staging environment for Payment Gateway v2 (ME region), we are noticing that subscriptions are not renewing automatically at the end of their term. Additionally, when we manually adjust a plan, the proration calculations are incorrect. This affects 5 test accounts. The low business impact is due to the staging nature, but we need to resolve this before pushing to production. Details: renewal dates are passing without status updates, and credit amounts on prorated invoices are negative."
  },
  {
   "i": 24530,
   "title": "SSO Integration Module: MFA missing, session expiry, and lockouts",
   "description": "We are seeing multiple issues with the SSO Integration Module in the EU-West production environment. First, users are not receiving the MFA prompt during login, allowing unauthorized access if credentials are leaked. Second, valid sessions are expiring unexpectedly, forcing frequent logins. Third, this has led to account lockouts for 23 users due to repeated failed authentication attempts caused by the session issues. This moderate impact needs immediate attention."
  },
  {
   "i": 24531,
   "title": "Help Center is down",
   "description": "Our Help Center seems to be having issues. We got some alerts about health checks failing and there might be an outage. It looks like some parts are down but others might work? Not sure of the exact scope or when it started. No users reported it yet but our internal tools flagged it. Please check."
  },
  {
   "i": 24532,
   "title": "Critical dependency timeouts affecting Tax Calculator",
   "description": "We are experiencing a critical outage with the Tax Calculator in the ANZ production region. The service is failing due to upstream dependency timeouts and errors. This is impacting over 11,900 users as tax calculations cannot be retrieved or applied. The dashboard shows a 100% failure rate for requests hitting the tax API endpoints. We need to identify which upstream service is failing and restore calculation capabilities immediately."
  },
  {
   "i": 24533,
   "title": "Audit log entries missing in Analytics Dashboard (Staging)",
   "description": "In the staging environment for the Analytics Dashboard (ANZ region), we have noticed that audit log entries are missing. We are not seeing records for specific data exports and filter applications that occurred in the last 48 hours. This affects 19 internal users and is a moderate impact because we cannot verify compliance with our data handling procedures during this phase. The logs appear to be truncating or failing to write entirely."
  },
  {
   "i": 24534,
   "title": "Corrupted exports and duplicate records in Funnel Analyzer",
   "description": "We are seeing data quality issues in the Funnel Analyzer production environment (LATAM region). When exporting funnel data, the files are often corrupted, or when they do open, they contain duplicate records for the same events. This affects 7 users who rely on these reports for weekly analysis. The impact is low as it is a reporting tool, but it undermines data confidence. Please investigate the export mechanism and deduplication logic."
  },
  {
   "i": 24535,
   "title": "SSO issues: Password reset links expired and missing emails",
   "description": "In the SSO Integration Module staging environment (EU-Central), we are encountering issues with the password reset flow. Links provided in emails are already expired when clicked. Furthermore, some users are not receiving the reset emails at all. Additionally, MFA prompts are sometimes not appearing after a successful reset. It is unclear if the email delivery system or the SSO module itself is failing to generate valid tokens or queue the messages. Impact is none currently as it is staging, but it blocks release."
  },
  {
   "i": 24536,
   "title": "Cache Service: Audit gaps, cert warnings, and privilege issues",
   "description": "We have a high-impact situation in the Cache Service production environment (ME region) affecting 111 users. Three distinct symptoms are observed: 1) Audit logs are missing entries for cache flush operations. 2) Users are seeing certificate warnings when connecting to the cache endpoints. 3) Elevated privileges have been observed for service accounts that should be read-only. These issues may be related or independent, but all require immediate investigation to ensure security and compliance."
  },
  {
   "i": 24537,
   "title": "SSO redirect loop in Identity Vault",
   "description": "Users are getting stuck in a redirect loop when trying to log in. The Identity Vault seems to be bouncing them back to the login page repeatedly. Some people can get in, others can't. It started recently. About 500 people might be affected. Please fix."
  },
  {
   "i": 24538,
   "title": "Data residency mismatch and missing audit logs in Wallet Service",
   "description": "In the staging environment for the Wallet Service (ANZ region), we are seeing a data residency flag mismatch where data is being tagged as stored in a different region than expected. Concurrently, audit logs are missing entries for specific wallet creation events. This affects 2 test accounts. The low business impact reflects the staging status, but this is a compliance blocker for our upcoming ANZ launch. We need to verify the residency tagging logic and the audit logging hooks."
  },
  {
   "i": 24539,
   "title": "Critical: Expired password reset links in Payment Gateway v2",
   "description": "We are facing a critical issue in the Payment Gateway v2 staging environment (US-West) where password reset links are consistently expiring before users can use them. This is blocking 1,281 test users from accessing the system to perform critical payment validations. The token expiration time seems to be set too low or the generation logic is flawed. This prevents us from completing our integration testing and is treated as high severity due to the volume of blocked accounts."
  }
